Question 1) Reverse Linked List
=========================================================
Brute Force Approach : reverse karna hai toh pehle stack mein daal denge aur uske baad stack se nikal ke linkedlist mein daal denge starting se 

code:class Solution {
    public ListNode reverseList(ListNode head) {
        Stack<Integer> st = new Stack<>();
        ListNode temp = head;
        while(temp!=null)
        {
            st.push(temp.val);
            temp = temp.next;
        }
        temp=head;
        while(temp!=null)
        {
            temp.val=st.pop();
            temp = temp.next;
        }
        return head;
    }
}

T.C. -> O(2N)
S.C. -> O(N) (for stack)

Optimal approach : with the help of 3 pointers we are reversing in place

code: class Solution {
    public ListNode reverseList(ListNode head) {
        ListNode temp = head, prev = null;
        while(temp != null)
        {
            ListNode front = temp.next;
            temp.next = prev;
            prev = temp;
            temp = front;
        }
        return prev;
    }
}

T.C. -> O(N)
S.C. -> O(1)

Recursive : sabse pehle sabse chota problem solve karo , uske baad usse bada problem solve karo , aise karne se hi logic banega aur every step pe dekho kya return ho raha hai
code: class Solution {
    public ListNode reverseList(ListNode head) {
        if(head==null || head.next==null) return head;
        ListNode newHead = reverseList(head.next);
        ListNode front = head.next;
        front.next = head;
        head.next = null;
        return newHead; 
    }
}

T.C. -> O(N)
S.C. -> O(N) (for recursion stack)

Question 2) Find the middle of LinkedList
Brute Force Approach: pehle total count nikal lo(size of ll) aur in case of both odd and evn ll , the middle will be at (n/2+1) toh ek aur loop lagake is element tak pahuch jao

code: class Solution {
    public ListNode middleNode(ListNode head) {
        if(head==null || head.next==null) return head;
        ListNode temp = head;
        int cnt = 0;
        while(temp!=null)
        {
            cnt+=1;
            temp=temp.next;
        }
        temp=head;
        int reach = (cnt/2+1);
        while(reach>1)
        {
            reach--;
            temp = temp.next;
        }
        return temp;
    }
}

T.C. -> O(N+N/2) one time full traversal and one time half traversal
S.C. -> O(1)

Optimal: Using Tortoise and Hare Algorithm(concept of slow and fast pointers)
code: class Solution {
    public ListNode middleNode(ListNode head) {
        if(head==null || head.next==null) return head;
        ListNode slow = head;
        ListNode fast = head;
        while(fast!=null && fast.next!=null)
        {
            slow=slow.next;
            fast=fast.next.next;
        }
        return slow;
    }
}

T.C. -> O(N/2)
S.C. -> O(1)

Intution behind this : If there are two people p1 and p2 , p1 is travelling with speed x and p2 is travelling with speed x/2
                       if p1 covers a distance of d , p2 covers a distance of d/2 . that's why it will at middle


Question 3)Merge two Sorted Lists

Note: Equal case me 2 nodes ek saath jodne se unke old next pointers reh jaate hain, jo cycle bana dete hain — isliye TLE aata hai.

BruteForce: Traverse through both ll and add into array and then sort the array and make ll through array

T.C. -> O(N)+O(N)+O(NlogN)+O(N)--> Two bigoh of N's for adding into array , sorting algorithm, converting from array to linkedlist
S.C. -> O(N) , an array to store all the elements

Optimal: with the help of dummy node and pointers 
code: class Solution {
    public ListNode mergeTwoLists(ListNode list1, ListNode list2) {
        if(list1==null && list2==null) return list1;
        ListNode Dummy = new ListNode(-1000);
        ListNode temp1 = list1, temp2 = list2;
        ListNode traversal = Dummy;
        while(temp1!=null && temp2!=null)
        {
            if(temp1.val<=temp2.val)
            {
                traversal.next=temp1;
                temp1=temp1.next;
            }
            else
            {
                traversal.next=temp2;
                temp2=temp2.next;
            }
            traversal=traversal.next;
        }
        if(temp1!=null)
        {
            traversal.next=temp1;
        }
        if(temp2!=null)
        {
            traversal.next=temp2;
        }
        return Dummy.next;
    }
}

T.C. -> O(N1+N2)
S.C. -> O(1)

Question 4)Remove N-th node from back of LinkedList
Striver Brute Force:
class Solution {
    public ListNode removeNthFromEnd(ListNode head, int n) {
        ListNode temp = head;
        int m = 0;
        int res = 0;
        while(temp!=null)
        {
            temp=temp.next;
            m+=1;
        }
        if(n==m) return head.next;
        temp = head;
        res = m-n;
        while(temp!=null)
        {
            res--;
            if(res==0) break;
            temp=temp.next;
        }
        temp.next = temp.next.next;
        return head;
    }
}

T.C. -> O(len) + O(len-N) , if n==1 toh last element delete karna padega toh both loops will run n times , so T.C. ->O(2N)
S.C. -> O(1)

